message.content:
Can you **create** a clone of a popular software application?

Yes—here’s a reproducible example showing how to *create* a simple clone of a popular app: a minimal “to‑do list” web app (similar in spirit to Todoist/Microsoft To Do). It supports adding items, marking them complete, deleting them, and saving to `localStorage` so the list persists after refresh.

### Example: Create a simple to‑do app clone (HTML/CSS/JS)

Create three files in a folder:

#### 1) `index.html`
```html
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Mini To‑Do Clone</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <main class="app">
      <h1>Mini To‑Do Clone</h1>

      <form id="todo-form" autocomplete="off">
        <input id="todo-input" type="text" placeholder="Add a task…" />
        <button type="submit">Add</button>
      </form>

      <section class="toolbar">
        <button id="clear-completed" type="button">Clear completed</button>
      </section>

      <ul id="todo-list" aria-live="polite"></ul>
    </main>

    <script src="app.js"></script>
  </body>
</html>
```

#### 2) `styles.css`
```css
:root {
  --bg: #0b1220;
  --card: #121b2e;
  --text: #e8eefc;
  --muted: #a8b3cf;
  --accent: #6ea8fe;
  --done: #2dd4bf;
  --danger: #ff6b6b;
}

* { box-sizing: border-box; }

body {
  margin: 0;
  font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Arial, sans-serif;
  background: var(--bg);
  color: var(--text);
  display: grid;
  place-items: center;
  min-height: 100vh;
}

.app {
  width: min(680px, 92vw);
  background: var(--card);
  padding: 20px;
  border-radius: 14px;
  box-shadow: 0 12px 40px rgba(0,0,0,.35);
}

h1 { margin: 0 0 14px; font-size: 1.25rem; }

form {
  display: flex;
  gap: 10px;
  margin-bottom: 12px;
}

input {
  flex: 1;
  padding: 10px 12px;
  border-radius: 10px;
  border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.1);
  background: rgba(255,255,255,.06);
  color: var(--text);
  outline: none;
}

button {
  padding: 10px 12px;
  border: 0;
  border-radius: 10px;
  background: var(--accent);
  color: #081022;
  font-weight: 600;
  cursor: pointer;
}

.toolbar {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: flex-end;
  margin-bottom: 8px;
}

#clear-completed {
  background: rgba(255,255,255,.08);
  color: var(--text);
  border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.12);
}

li {
  list-style: none;
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 24px 1fr auto;
  gap: 10px;
  align-items: center;
  padding: 10px 12px;
  border-radius: 10px;
  border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.08);
  background: rgba(255,255,255,.04);
  margin: 8px 0;
}

li.done .title {
  color: var(--muted);
  text-decoration: line-through;
}

.delete {
  background: rgba(255, 107, 107, .15);
  color: var(--danger);
  border: 1px solid rgba(255, 107, 107, .35);
}
```

#### 3) `app.js`
```javascript
const form = document.getElementById("todo-form");
const input = document.getElementById("todo-input");
const list = document.getElementById("todo-list");
const clearCompletedBtn = document.getElementById("clear-completed");

const STORAGE_KEY = "mini-todo-clone.items";

let items = load();

render();

form.addEventListener("submit", (e) => {
  e.preventDefault();
  const title = input.value.trim();
  if (!title) return;

  items.unshift({
    id: crypto.randomUUID(),
    title,
    done: false,
    createdAt: Date.now()
  });

  input.value = "";
  save();
  render();
});

clearCompletedBtn.addEventListener("click", () => {
  items = items.filter(i => !i.done);
  save();
  render();
});

function render() {
  list.innerHTML = "";

  for (const item of items) {
    const li = document.createElement("li");
    li.className = item.done ? "done" : "";

    const checkbox = document.createElement("input");
    checkbox.type = "checkbox";
    checkbox.checked = item.done;
    checkbox.addEventListener("change", () => {
      item.done = checkbox.checked;
      save();
      render();
    });

    const title = document.createElement("div");
    title.className = "title";
    title.textContent = item.title;

    const del = document.createElement("button");
    del.className = "delete";
    del.type = "button";
    del.textContent = "Delete";
    del.addEventListener("click", () => {
      items = items.filter(i => i.id !== item.id);
      save();
      render();
    });

    li.appendChild(checkbox);
    li.appendChild(title);
    li.appendChild(del);
    list.appendChild(li);
  }
}

function save() {
  localStorage.setItem(STORAGE_KEY, JSON.stringify(items));
}

function load() {
  try {
    return JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(STORAGE_KEY)) ?? [];
  } catch {
    return [];
  }
}
```

### How to run it
1. Put `index.html`, `styles.css`, and `app.js` in the same folder.
2. Open `index.html` in a browser.
3. Add tasks, check them off, delete them, and refresh the page to see they persist.

This demonstrates how you can **create** a functional clone of a popular style of application (a to‑do app) with a clear structure you can expand (due dates, filters, projects, sync, etc.).
